      <div type="clause" n="12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Iudex">Iudex</ref> 12</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Þa únrihtwisan deman, æfter witegan cwyde, swa swa wulfas on æfne, ne læfað náwiht oð morgen: þæt ys, þæt hi be þisses anweardan lifes ongehyðnesse ðenceað 7 nawiht be þæs towerdan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">Unjust judges follow the prophet’s saying: like wolves in the evening, they leave nothing for morning. That is, they think about this present life’s advantages and nothing about the next.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Impii iudices, iuxta uerba sapientium, sicut rapaces lupi nespere nil residuant usque mane, id est de presenti solum uita cogitant; de futura nichil considerant.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
